    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey can u give me a quick checklist for wcag 2.1 compliance? mostly looking for stuff on color contrast ratios and making sure screen readers work right for a new fintech app we're building",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sure thing! When it comes to WCAG 2.1 compliance, especially for color contrast ratios and screen reader compatibility, here's a quick checklist for your fintech app:\n\n1. **Color Contrast Ratios**: Ensure that your app's color contrast ratios meet the minimum requirements of 4.5:1 for normal text and 3:1 for large text. You can use tools like the WebAIM Color Contrast Checker to verify this.\n\n2. **Screen Reader Compatibility**: Make sure all interactive elements are accessible to screen readers. Use ARIA (Accessible Rich Internet Applications) labels and roles to describe elements and actions.\n\n3. **Keyboard Navigation**: Ensure that all functionality is accessible via keyboard alone. This includes being able to navigate menus, forms, and other interactive elements without a mouse.\n\n4. **Text Alternatives**: Provide text alternatives (alt text) for non-text content, such as images and charts, so screen readers can convey the information to users.\n\n5. **Error Identification and Recovery**: Clearly identify and describe errors in form fields, and provide suggestions for correction. This helps users understand and fix issues without frustration.\n\n6. **Consistent Navigation**: Maintain consistent navigation throughout the app to help users understand and",
      "source": "target",
